## Summary

**5C §2.5 — re-alarm loop wiring (final slice), done and committed.**

- Wired the previously-built `MorningRealarmPolicy` into real call sites: `MorningAlarmStoppedIntent.perform()` (schedules on Stop when no capture yet), `MorningRitualCoordinator.captureCompleted` (cancels + resets on capture), and `disableImmediately()` (clears dangling reservations on disable).
- **Caught a real design bug myself before committing**, not just trusting Codex's first pass: it chained re-alarms one Stop-tap at a time, but nothing re-invokes that intent when a plain notification later fires — so at most 1 of the spec'd 3 attempts would ever have fired. Sent it back with the fix (plan all 3 occurrences up front, replaying the existing pure policy).
- `swift-reviewer` then caught **two real HIGH concurrency findings** in the redo (an un-awaited cleanup callback risking account-deletion teardown races, and a counter-persistence race vs. concurrent disable). Sent both back to Codex, fixed, re-verified.
- Independently ran `xcodebuild test -only-testing:SkyGridTests` myself (not Codex's self-report) after each round: **261/261 green**, both times.
- `.loop/verify.sh` correctly returns rc=1 — 5 VISION.md TODO items still open, not a false green.

**Next step queued in VISION.md**: §2.6 (the exact approved alarm-copy block) — last remaining 5C sub-step, then 6C, then 3B's client display.
